      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Think what you want, but I happen to know he is 100% sight-reading on them.  He's sight reading plus improvising over them.  The Ghosts & Goblins one was the first one I saw from him, actually.  Also, in terms of sloppiness, he's playing on an out of tune piano, sight-reading, in a style in which it's more important to keep the pace going, rather than worry about if he misses a note here or there, and keep the pace going he does!  Look at some of his original works - they're much cleaner.  \n\n\n[quote=\"\"Adam\"\"]\n\nThat's partially true. If you keep looking at youtube, a lot of these pieces you can see \"people have brought\" to him before, he's got much rougher versions of nearly every song on there. While he's still immensely skilled at playing and improvising, I doubt he's sight-reading 100% on any of them. Not that it can't be done, I just think it's suspicious that he's brought the same obscure video game sheet music to sight read every time he's at a public piano with a video camera present. Mario? Sure. 3 different Mario songs? Maybe, ok. Ghosts n' Goblins? Unlikely. Still, I'd like to see Root Beer Rag out of him, the only ones on youtube are super sloppy.\n\n[/quote]",
